with 10 series and over 700 episodes  it's only natural that star trek has  messed up a few times over the years  whether they're continuity errors  editing blunders wardrobe screw-ups or  other oversights here are some of the  biggest on-screen mistakes you'll find  in star trek tv shows  23rd century con man harry mudd is one  of the first recurring villains in star  trek the original series  in the season 1 episode muds women mud  beams aboard the enterprise accompanied  by a trio of women whose beauty leaves  both scotty and  mccoy dumbstruck dr mccoy's arousal  isn't the only thing worth noticing  about his appearance in this scene  when he first sees the women mccoy is  wearing his bridge uniform which  includes a light blue shirt with a dark  blue collar the camera cuts to mud's  alluring ladies and when it returns to  mccoy he's wearing the medical smock he  usually reserves for sickbay duty  there are also windows behind him  indicating he's in a completely  different part of the ship  the next time we see mccoy he's back in  the transporter room  wearing his bridge uniform apparently  whoever edited mud's women didn't think  mccoy looked aroused enough so they used  archival footage of him without caring  about where he was  or what he was wearing either that or  the space-time continuum was acting  really weird that day  one of the more interesting season one  episodes of star trek deep space nine  is dramatist personae in which a  contagion renders the entire crew  power hungry and violent except for  constable odo  the crew soon splits into warring  factions and after commander cisco  survives a botched assassination attempt  he tries to escape the  station with chief o'brien one of the  first things they do is throw away their  starfleet communicator badges  so that no one can track them as the  only member of the senior crew who isn't  losing his mind  odo manages to manipulate both parties  into a cargo bay where he can blast the  contagion  into the void of space odo warns  everyone to hold on to something before  opening the bay door and cisco  still without a combadge grabs a cargo  container we then see several shots of  different crew members fighting the pull  of the vacuum  once odo closes the door the camera  turns to cisco whose calm badge has  inexplicably reappeared on his uniform  why i have no idea  you could try to explain this by saying  that the com badge's return symbolizes  cisco's return to sanity but  otherwise it's an obvious goof  yesterday's enterprise is one of the  most beloved  episodes of star trek the next  generation the story  changes the trek timeline with wharf  absent from the enterprise tasha yar  still alive and the federation stuck  in a losing war with the klingons among  other changes the enterprise's interior  is a lot darker and the crew's uniforms  have changed this isn't right  it's changed the timeline is restored  thanks to the intervention of the  enigmatic gainen who senses something is  wrong and convinces captain picard to  help restore their reality  yesterday's enterprise ends with gainen  and jordy talking intent forward  gainen asks the chief engineer to tell  her about tasha yar  someone she never met in the original  timeline but for some reason jordy is  still wearing his uniform from the  alternate  enterprise we know this because of the  black cuffs on his sleeves which aren't  a feature of his normal uniform  unless this is a subtle hint that gainen  never really succeeded in fixing the  timeline  someone should have told jordy he was in  the wrong duds  seriously seriously a lot of things  change on star trek voyager  after the introduction of the reformed  borg crew member  seven of nine because of her issues with  trust and isolation  seven is rarely seen fraternizing with  voyager's crew  instead we usually find her working  alone in the astrometrics lab  unfortunately the increased role of the  astrometrics lab  leads to a bit of confusion in season  seven's  shattered commander chocote finds  himself thrown back in time to an  earlier version of voyager  when he tells captain janeway that they  need to get to the astrometrics lab she  responds that voyager doesn't have one  implying it hasn't been built yet  voyager doesn't have an astrometrics lab  but this isn't the case while we never  see the astrometrics lab before seven  comes on board  it was always a part of the ship in  season four's revulsion chicote  orders kim and seven to update the lab  because it hasn't been upgraded since  before the events of the series premiere  how could it have been upgraded if it  didn't exist  it's a long story one of the most unique  episodes of star trek enterprise is  season two's carbon  creek a huge chunk of it doesn't even  feature the regular cast  jolene blaylock does double duty playing  both the vulcan first officer to paul  and topal's ancestor tamir de paul tells  the story of how a small group of  vulcans  including tamir crashed in the united  states in the 1950s and were forced to  pose as humans  would you like to hear the story tamir  initially tries to keep her distance  from the earthlings around her but  eventually finds herself becoming  sympathetic  to them and even involved in their lives  just as scottie sells the secret of  transparent aluminum in star trek iv  the voyage home tamir takes a trip to  pittsburgh in 1957  and sells the secret of velcro so she  can help a human boy pay for his college  tuition  the only problem with this detail is  that not only did someone else invent  velcro  but it was patented in 1952 and was  already in use in the united states by  1957.  obviously 50s kids weren't securing  their sneakers with it yet  but it was still out there do you  realize you've just rewritten our  history books  father-son relationships are a major  theme in ds9  usually represented by the love between  ben cisco and his son jake  but in a season 4 two-parter that  relationship expands to include ben's  father  joseph cisco we meet the stubborn but  charismatic restaurant owner when ben is  summoned to earth to brief starfleet on  the growing threat of the dominion  the only problem is that earlier in the  series we're led to believe joseph cisco  is dead ben never outright says he's  deceased but  all the statements he makes about his  father before season 4 strongly imply  he's already passed on  for example in both the series premiere  and season two's paradise  ben refers to his father in the past  tense he says  well my father was a chef also in season  two's the alternate  ben tells odo of an illness his father  suffered strongly implying he died from  it  ds9 never provides an explanation for  this discrepancy but regardless  joseph is a beloved character who  continued to appear in the series  regularly and were glad he was around to  see it through  you up for a stroll with your old man  i can't think of anything i'd rather do  written by the acclaimed science fiction  author harlan ellison the city on the  edge of forever is often considered one  of the best  episodes of any star trek series as well  as one of the saddest episodes in the  franchise  but even here there's a blink and you'll  miss it error that could take you out of  the story pretty fast  the story transports mccoy spock and  captain kirk back in time to the great  depression  kirk and spock's search for mccoy whose  actions they fear have deeply harmed  the timeline the pair secure an  apartment as their base of operations  and it's this apartment building that  provides the episode with its goof  we have a flop we have a white cap a  place to sleep  after a scene in which a homeless man  accidentally vaporizes himself with  mccoy's phaser the camera cuts to the  exterior of kirk and spock's building  on the right side of the building you  can clearly see a yellow sign indicating  that the structure contains a bomb  shelter in case of nuclear attack  such signs didn't exis